      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5457311549295775,
        "y0": 0.11294903904551735,
        "x1": 0.9238580700845066,
        "y1": 0.12027351945443573
      },
      "text": "Presede into the plumpe and with a prynce metes.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6890463098591549,
        "y0": 0.1253412117958622,
        "x1": 0.9566464723380281,
        "y1": 0.1327177044578106
      },
      "text": "3forte Arthui-e, MS. Lincoln, f. 76.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5473505352112676,
        "y0": 0.1368799900537932,
        "x1": 0.9562456757183098,
        "y1": 0.15780602748112946
      },
      "text": "When kynge Richard perceved that the people by plumpes fled from hym to Duke Henry.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8076659154929576,
        "y0": 0.1639736186027587,
        "x1": 0.955434366197183,
        "y1": 0.1699447184759609
      },
      "text": "Hall's Union, 1548.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5254889014084506,
        "y0": 0.1741749682758622,
        "x1": 0.8445068169014083,
        "y1": 0.1857294819001152
      },
      "text": "A pump ; a draw-well. Comw.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5250840563380281,
        "y0": 0.18828394580827587,
        "x1": 0.7773065836619719,
        "y1": 0.19911030948632208
      },
      "text": "(5) A hard blow. far. dial.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5250840563380281,
        "y0": 0.20431776034482768,
        "x1": 0.9550295211267604,
        "y1": 0.2249551777491016
      },
      "text": "(6) Directly ; exactly. Var. dial. Forby has plumpendicular, perpendicular.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.524274366197183,
        "y0": 0.2289068746151725,
        "x1": 0.9570537464788732,
        "y1": 0.29216476697686977
      },
      "text": "PLUM-PORRIDGE. Porridge with plums in it, a favourite dish at Christmas in some parts of the country. It is mentioned as part of Christmas fare in the Humourist, ed. 1724, p. 22, and by Addison.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5238695211267604,
        "y0": 0.29559358896551735,
        "x1": 0.8947148928450704,
        "y1": 0.3061322508731955
      },
      "text": "PLUMP-PATE. A thick-headed fellow.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.523464676056338,
        "y0": 0.3091082842979311,
        "x1": 0.8121192112676054,
        "y1": 0.3195635652760266
      },
      "text": "PLUMPY. To churn. Comw.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5230598309859154,
        "y0": 0.3222662963255174,
        "x1": 0.8157579587605635,
        "y1": 0.33262564750095497
      },
      "text": "PLUMTEN. Plunged. Weber.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5230598309859154,
        "y0": 0.3363475111186207,
        "x1": 0.9546214372957746,
        "y1": 0.4271217188682047
      },
      "text": "PLUM-TREE. The female pudendum. Have at the plum tree seems to have been either the burden of a song or a proverbial phrase. It occurs in Middleton, although Mr. Dyce does not seem to be acquainted with the meaning of the term itself, which may be gathered from Cotgrave, in v. Hoche-prunier, and the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5449214647887324,
        "y0": 0.4323846297075863,
        "x1": 0.8813444795492958,
        "y1": 0.4406891199828168
      },
      "text": "Mariage of Witt and Wisdome, p. 16.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5222501408450704,
        "y0": 0.4440414219089655,
        "x1": 0.8736483747605635,
        "y1": 0.45420516234060193
      },
      "text": "PLUNGE. (1) A deep pool. Somerset.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.522654985915493,
        "y0": 0.45737063419172425,
        "x1": 0.8295356461971828,
        "y1": 0.4679658267277014
      },
      "text": "(2) A strait or difficulty. Greene.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5218452957746479,
        "y0": 0.47095060318344834,
        "x1": 0.8299356331267602,
        "y1": 0.4812083966036249
      },
      "text": "PLUNGY. Wet; rainy. {A.-N)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5218452957746479,
        "y0": 0.4843063640193104,
        "x1": 0.8611103229295773,
        "y1": 0.494489549614883
      },
      "text": "PLUNKET. A coarse woollen cloth.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5214404507042253,
        "y0": 0.4979600514593104,
        "x1": 0.8886308811267607,
        "y1": 0.507693713104047
      },
      "text": "PLUNKY. Short ; thick ; heavy. East.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5214404507042253,
        "y0": 0.5111583596013795,
        "x1": 0.9517907605633804,
        "y1": 0.5344515447225087
      },
      "text": "PLUNT. A walking-stick, generally one which has a large knob. Glouc.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.5390215591917242,
        "x1": 0.8594860845070423,
        "y1": 0.5481420374670248
      },
      "text": "PLURISY. Superabundance. Shak.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.5523020305710346,
        "x1": 0.9497624867605631,
        "y1": 0.5748922219775824
      },
      "text": "PLUSHES. The thin hoops which hold a besom together. West.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.5800662665517242,
        "x1": 0.9501713802816901,
        "y1": 0.601983312557884
      },
      "text": "PLY. To bend ; to consent, or comply. Still in use in Dorset, Barnes's Gl.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.6057987031572415,
        "x1": 0.8169773521126759,
        "y1": 0.6156603772010899
      },
      "text": "PLYER. A very common bawd.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5194162253521126,
        "y0": 0.6191795307434482,
        "x1": 0.9505762253521125,
        "y1": 0.65609049844632
      },
      "text": "PLYMOUTH-CLOAK. A cane, or stick. So called, says Ray, '· because we use a staff in cuerpo, but not when we wear a cloak.\"",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5194162253521126,
        "y0": 0.6591060717241379,
        "x1": 0.7558489852394366,
        "y1": 0.6695472300553698
      },
      "text": "PO. A peacock. {A.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.616579042253521,
        "y0": 0.674607646497931,
        "x1": 0.8072643091830984,
        "y1": 0.6948090947147438
      },
      "text": "A pruest proud ase a po, Seththe weddeth us bo.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.707264338028169,
        "y0": 0.7007895698813793,
        "x1": 0.9497665352112675,
        "y1": 0.7073645103785429
      },
      "text": "Wright's Political Songs, p. 159.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5186065352112675,
        "y0": 0.7124667158082759,
        "x1": 0.9501713802816901,
        "y1": 0.7223753487725454
      },
      "text": "POACHED. Land is said to he poached vihtn it",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.518201690140845,
        "y0": 0.7297927713793104,
        "x1": 0.9449156815774645,
        "y1": 0.7494233801837421
      },
      "text": "is trodden with holes by heavy cattle. Var.diat. POACHING. Swampy. Devon.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.518201690140845,
        "y0": 0.7534988897931034,
        "x1": 0.9501746190422534,
        "y1": 0.7758242736132142
      },
      "text": "POAD-MILK. The first milk given by cows after calving. Sussex.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.518201690140845,
        "y0": 0.7805389752082759,
        "x1": 0.9497697739718308,
        "y1": 0.8031559004966833
      },
      "text": "POARE-BLIND. Dim-sighted. The word occurs in Hollyband's Dictionarie, 1593.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.518201690140845,
        "y0": 0.8077337281227586,
        "x1": 0.7619200419154931,
        "y1": 0.8163772670279634
      },
      "text": "POAT. To kick. Devon.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.518201690140845,
        "y0": 0.8214556528275861,
        "x1": 0.5777139154929579,
        "y1": 0.8299825987980922
      },
      "text": "POBS.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6011949295774648,
        "y0": 0.8228218799268966,
        "x1": 0.6829793016338024,
        "y1": 0.8293319421464196
      },
      "text": "Porridge.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7092885633802816,
        "y0": 0.8226937609806896,
        "x1": 0.7744629518873241,
        "y1": 0.8293639209612916
      },
      "text": "Craven.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5186065352112675,
        "y0": 0.8335371871875862,
        "x1": 0.7971439921126762,
        "y1": 0.8436877332785988
      },
      "text": "POCHE. A pocket. {A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5781187605633803,
        "y0": 0.8478446271724138,
        "x1": 0.843291472,
        "y1": 0.8564215569198464
      },
      "text": "Unto another she dyde as moche ;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5777139154929577,
        "y0": 0.8601105196013793,
        "x1": 0.8874139168450709,
        "y1": 0.8668063589603947
      },
      "text": "For they love none but for theyr poche.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5186065352112675,
        "y0": 0.8722357597089656,
        "x1": 0.9501794771830994,
        "y1": 0.8928497898564881
      },
      "text": "The Complaynte of them that ben to late Maryed. POCHEE. A dish in ancient cookery consisting",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5404681690140845,
        "y0": 0.8988972370855173,
        "x1": 0.872841113690141,
        "y1": 0.9059319899268089
      },
      "text": "principally of poached eggs. Pegge.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5190113802816901,
        "y0": 0.9099704418372414,
        "x1": 0.7169903359999997,
        "y1": 0.9193605235631293
      },
      "text": "POCHERS. Potters?",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5190113802816901,
        "y0": 0.9227427044289654,
        "x1": 0.8400454242253521,
        "y1": 0.9328932505199781
      },
      "text": "POCHIN. A hedgehog. Somerset.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5190113802816901,
        "y0": 0.9363547031572413,
        "x1": 0.8133377949295773,
        "y1": 0.9462323238967162
      },
      "text": "POCHIT. A pollard tree. Line.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
